# dsh-kit.conf - what THIS project carries into the UCL Data Safe Haven, and how it is
# installed there. Copy to dsh-kit.conf (or let the dsh-init skill write it) and fill in.
#
# One file, read on both sides of the airlock: by the workstation scripts that build the
# payload, and - because build_payload.sh carries it - by the scripts inside that unpack,
# mirror and install it. Nothing else in this repo names your packages.
#
# Format: plain KEY="value" lines, nothing else. No $expansion, no command substitution,
# no arrays - lists are space-separated. It is parsed, not sourced, so bash and
# PowerShell read it identically and nothing in it can run.

# A short name for the project. Used for the default workspace directory inside
# (~/Scratch/<project> on the Linux cluster) and in log headers.
KIT_PROJECT="my-project"

# The git repositories carried in, BASE FIRST: a repo must come after every repo it
# depends on. Each name is a directory basename, which is also its GitLab project name
# inside.
KIT_REPOS="my-library my-analysis"

# Where those repositories are checked out on THIS machine. Relative paths are relative
# to the directory this file is in. A repo whose directory is not under here can be
# exported by path: export_bundles.sh --package /path/to/repo
KIT_REPOS_DIR="../"

# Repos that are EDITED inside the DSH (notebooks, run scripts) rather than mirrored.
# A mirror is read-only inside and a local edit there is a fault; a working repo is
# overwritten by the payload when the payload carries it, with local edits parked on a
# dsh-local/<stamp> branch first. Must be a subset of KIT_REPOS. Usually empty.
KIT_WORKING_REPOS=""

# How the repos are installed inside.
#   venv       one .venv, every repo installed editable in one `uv pip install` call,
#              so first-party names resolve to the local checkouts. The default.
#   workspace  a uv workspace: a root pyproject.toml listing every repo as a member,
#              synced with `uv sync --all-packages`. Use it if you already work in a
#              uv workspace outside. A pyproject.dsh.toml beside this file, if present,
#              is carried and used as the root verbatim instead of the generated one.
KIT_INSTALL_MODE="venv"

# Extras to install, as requirement specs naming a repo:  "my-library[plots,fast]".
# Repos not named here are installed without extras.
KIT_EXTRAS=""

# The Python the venv is built with must satisfy this. Checked against the interpreter
# the probe finds; it does NOT pick one for you.
KIT_PYTHON_SPEC=">=3.11, <3.14"

# Smoke tests run after install. Import names default to every repo name with - -> _;
# list them explicitly if a repo's import name differs from its directory name.
KIT_IMPORT_CHECK=""
# Console scripts (from [project.scripts]) that must run with --help. Optional.
KIT_CONSOLE_SCRIPTS=""

# GitLab inside the DSH, where the bundles are mirrored and everything is cloned from.
KIT_GITLAB_HOST="gitlab.idhs.ucl.ac.uk"
# The group (or your username, for a personal namespace) the projects live under.
KIT_GITLAB_GROUP="<gitlab-group>"
# Optional: a different namespace for KIT_WORKING_REPOS, e.g. your personal one when
# the mirrors live in a shared group.
KIT_WORKING_NAMESPACE=""

# Which boxes this project uses: dsh-vm (the Windows analysis desktop) and/or
# dsh-cluster (the Linux batch cluster, reached from the VM). The payload carries
# only what these need.
KIT_TARGETS="dsh-vm"
